WEBVTT

00:01.210 --> 00:03.003
How's it coming along?

00:03.754 --> 00:04.880
Which one?

00:04.880 --> 00:08.634
You know, the one we moved up
because of the teaser.

00:08.634 --> 00:12.429
Oh, that one where the deadline
got insanely moved up.

00:12.429 --> 00:14.516
I already apologized for that.

00:14.516 --> 00:15.641
So, what now?

00:15.641 --> 00:18.685
Should we stop accepting
new song requests?

00:18.685 --> 00:20.771
It's fine. I'll make it work.

00:20.771 --> 00:21.980
I knew you would!

00:21.980 --> 00:25.526
I just sent the melody.
Let me know if it works.

00:25.526 --> 00:27.611
Thanks! You're the best!

00:27.611 --> 00:29.030
All right, meeting over...

00:29.030 --> 00:30.781
Hold on!

00:31.907 --> 00:35.159
Be honest.
How do you feel about MewType?

00:35.744 --> 00:38.037
H... how do I feel?

00:38.037 --> 00:41.542
You didn't seem very into it.

00:41.542 --> 00:42.918
- Yeah...
- Still!

00:42.918 --> 00:47.673
I really believe your melodies
come alive with a full band sound.

00:51.843 --> 00:55.722
Isn't there someone else
you should be more worried about?

00:55.722 --> 00:57.140
Like the singer.

00:57.140 --> 00:58.308
Nakamachi-san?

00:58.308 --> 01:00.819
Right. She won't sing, right?

01:00.819 --> 01:01.853
Oh, yeah.

01:01.853 --> 01:05.899
Band or whatever, it's work,
so I'll do my part.

01:05.899 --> 01:09.069
But with a singer like that,
there's a limit.

01:09.069 --> 01:11.343
She's dealing with her own issues.

01:11.343 --> 01:12.364
"Issues"?

01:13.031 --> 01:17.077
She used to be in another group
under the name "Erea."

01:17.077 --> 01:19.371
It ended up being a terrible experience.

01:20.334 --> 01:23.297
Then why'd you put her in the band?

01:23.297 --> 01:24.501
It was her choice.

01:25.002 --> 01:28.255
She wanted to change,
to make things better for herself,

01:28.255 --> 01:30.465
so she took the agency's offer.

01:31.925 --> 01:34.595
Please be patient with her.

01:38.473 --> 01:40.851
- I'll think about it.
- Thanks!

01:48.800 --> 01:50.235
A terrible experience, huh?

01:57.021 --> 01:58.243
All right.

01:58.806 --> 02:00.120
Let's do this.

02:08.962 --> 02:13.550
ready set and find out ready set and find out
it's only one newtype

02:14.742 --> 02:19.474
The story always revolves around us

02:19.474 --> 02:24.228
That may be a given, but let me repeat it

02:24.228 --> 02:29.400
Can you read the guidelines?
No matter how carefully we write them

02:29.400 --> 02:34.446
Why does something always get in the way?
Still, we'll make it roar!

02:34.446 --> 02:38.532
In a heartbeat, like an overdrive

02:38.532 --> 02:45.083
We yearn to distort the world we see

02:45.083 --> 02:50.255
Seeing too clearly makes innocence
seem ridiculous, what a joke!

02:50.255 --> 02:55.008
Even vain attempts at being brave
Will be rewarded when the time comes

02:55.008 --> 02:58.845
This is the plot of our survival

02:58.845 --> 03:04.519
Rewriting the tale
Shedding absurd tears, the newtype way

03:04.519 --> 03:09.606
We can go anywhere, we can, so don't stop now

03:09.606 --> 03:13.860
Not an anime, not real either,
let's make our own category

03:13.860 --> 03:17.273
We've grown tired
of this complicated, dull world!

03:17.273 --> 03:20.575
Leave it to us, we'll write our own dreams

03:20.575 --> 03:23.954
ready set and find out ready set and find out
it's only one newtype, our choice

03:23.954 --> 03:25.538
Following the steady beat

03:25.538 --> 03:31.002
ready set and find out ready set and find out
it's only one newtype

03:31.002 --> 03:38.510
(Shiroyama)

03:41.422 --> 03:42.556
Arale-chan!

03:44.761 --> 03:45.934
Miyako-chan!

03:45.934 --> 03:49.379
I'm inviting you to a super fun lunch!

03:53.393 --> 03:58.071
An anpan bakery!
The first shop and the second one.

04:02.075 --> 04:03.910
An anpan folder shop.

04:03.910 --> 04:07.539
Now, buy two eligible items
at participating stores

04:07.539 --> 04:11.418
and get a Magilulu plastic folder
of your choice!

04:11.418 --> 04:14.713
You can even get
High-power Meat as a snack...

04:16.339 --> 04:18.008
Uh...

04:18.508 --> 04:21.887
Nono-chan-san, do you like anpan?

04:21.887 --> 04:24.014
I love it!

04:26.057 --> 04:30.937
I kind of went overboard buying them
for the plastic folders.

04:30.937 --> 04:36.109
So, well, could you help me
eat a few of them, maybe?

04:36.109 --> 04:38.737
Sure, all right!

04:38.737 --> 04:40.725
Leave it to me!

04:42.004 --> 04:43.366
How about you, Miyako-san?

04:44.159 --> 04:45.994
I'm fine.

04:45.994 --> 04:49.706
Looks like it's frozen bread
for me until next week.

04:50.415 --> 04:52.334
Let's dig in!

04:55.529 --> 04:57.782
It's yummy.

04:59.883 --> 05:02.093
I wish I'd gotten milk too.

05:02.093 --> 05:05.699
But I bought too much bread,
so I need to save money.

05:05.699 --> 05:07.346
Do you like milk?

05:07.346 --> 05:09.601
I usually don't care much.

05:09.601 --> 05:13.438
But anpan and milk together?
Isn't it the best?!

05:13.438 --> 05:15.148
I've never tried it.

05:16.107 --> 05:19.069
You get this, right, Miyako-san?

05:19.069 --> 05:22.072
I'm not really a fan of milk...

05:22.072 --> 05:25.450
Instead, I like pairing anpan
with green tea.

05:25.450 --> 05:26.369
For sure!

05:26.369 --> 05:29.955
I can almost see a tea room
just by imagining it.

05:29.955 --> 05:32.040
I'll brew some tea tomorrow.

05:32.040 --> 05:34.584
What about orange juice and anpan?

05:34.584 --> 05:38.296
The sourness of the orange
goes well with the red bean paste.

05:38.296 --> 05:40.549
It makes it so sweet!

05:41.299 --> 05:48.265
And the sweetness of the red bean paste
brings out the orange's tangy punch!

05:49.516 --> 05:50.392
Look!

05:50.392 --> 05:52.561
Yuno-chan's new song!

05:52.561 --> 05:53.854
Oh, that's true.

05:53.854 --> 05:55.648
"Song contribution"?

05:55.648 --> 05:59.276
Have you two ever seen
Yuno-chan outside?

06:00.536 --> 06:01.865
Me neither.

06:03.029 --> 06:08.952
I really love Yuno-chan,
so I sent her a whole bunch.

06:08.952 --> 06:10.395
Sent her what?

06:10.395 --> 06:12.289
(Matching bedheads!)
A pineapple.

06:12.798 --> 06:14.541
(Human Pigeon)
Pigeons.

06:14.541 --> 06:17.335
- And a swamp.
- A swamp?!

06:17.335 --> 06:20.755
Every time,
I would get a reply instantly.

06:20.755 --> 06:24.509
"Indeed, bedhead can sometimes
look like a pineapple."

06:24.509 --> 06:28.430
"Indeed, pigeons are very cute
when they fly."

06:28.430 --> 06:32.642
"Indeed, it is worrying when bath water
looks like a swamp."

06:32.642 --> 06:35.948
I've uncovered the truth.

06:35.948 --> 06:37.855
"The truth"?

06:37.855 --> 06:39.064
Right...

06:42.152 --> 06:43.904
Singularity...

06:43.904 --> 06:45.279
Singu-what?

06:45.279 --> 06:49.337
Advanced AI exceeding
human-level intelligence.

06:49.337 --> 06:50.368
Yes!

06:50.368 --> 06:53.704
One! We've only seen her
on the VRFloor.

06:53.704 --> 06:56.499
Two! She always has a mountain of work.

06:56.499 --> 07:00.796
Three! She sends instant cold replies.

07:00.796 --> 07:02.255
Which means...

07:02.696 --> 07:05.866
It means that
Yuno-chan's true identity is...

07:06.509 --> 07:11.148
a high-spec composing AI robot
made by some amazing company.

07:11.148 --> 07:13.850
Wh... what?!

07:15.923 --> 07:17.020
Am I sick?

07:18.939 --> 07:20.471
I see.

07:21.274 --> 07:24.611
Mrs. Nonholmes, she looks human to me.

07:24.611 --> 07:28.156
No need to rush, my dear Aralen.
If we can't tell by looking...

07:29.741 --> 07:31.952
Touch her!

07:32.851 --> 07:33.954
Oh, this is...

07:33.954 --> 07:35.830
Did you get something?

07:35.830 --> 07:37.540
I've got nothing.

07:37.540 --> 07:40.168
- It's a dead end!
- You're in the way.

07:40.168 --> 07:43.546
Now, now. Take a look at this.

07:44.631 --> 07:47.968
- What's this?
- Select all images with traffic lights.

07:48.468 --> 07:51.329
Select all images with traffic lights.

07:54.808 --> 07:56.643
You did it!

07:56.643 --> 07:59.129
Select all images with a guitar.

08:01.147 --> 08:02.190
You did it!

08:02.190 --> 08:04.651
Select all images with Mokeme Aliens.

08:05.485 --> 08:07.028
She froze.

08:07.028 --> 08:08.655
I knew she was a robot.

08:08.655 --> 08:10.865
This can't be...

08:10.865 --> 08:13.910
If Sengoku-san really is a robot,

08:13.910 --> 08:17.163
a manga-drawing robot
might show up someday too.

08:17.163 --> 08:20.709
One that can analyze trends,
doesn't need sleep,

08:20.709 --> 08:23.003
talks smoothly, sings, dances...

08:23.003 --> 08:25.005
If that happens...

08:26.141 --> 08:29.467
Humans lose! Unemployment! No escape?!

08:29.467 --> 08:31.052
What? Unemployment?!

08:31.636 --> 08:34.222
Nono-chan-san! Miyako-san's in trouble!

08:35.223 --> 08:37.809
- Check for eye bags.
- Checking.

08:37.809 --> 08:40.979
Okay, relax.

08:40.979 --> 08:43.023
Doctor, look at this!

08:44.399 --> 08:46.026
Are you done?

08:46.026 --> 08:47.861
Let's practice.

08:53.366 --> 08:56.453
(Starting with this song?
(Sounds promising)

08:56.453 --> 08:59.539
(Clematis on guitar
is absolutely the best...)

09:00.429 --> 09:01.332
Thank you guys for all the comments.
Now, onto the next song...

09:01.332 --> 09:03.270
(I came back after a week, )
Thank you guys for all the comments.

09:03.270 --> 09:05.253
(and she's gotten insanely good!)
Now, onto the next song...

09:05.253 --> 09:07.744
(New here! Play Roselia's
'Determination Symphony'!)

09:07.744 --> 09:09.006
(New here! Play Roselia's
'Determination Symphony'!) I'm sorry.

09:09.006 --> 09:14.011
I have to clear the rights,
so it's hard to change the setlist.

09:14.511 --> 09:15.388
(Please! Just the chorus!)

09:15.388 --> 09:17.390
(Please! Just the chorus!)
I don't think I can...

09:19.267 --> 09:22.270
(Viola:
They're tipping you, just play it)

09:24.272 --> 09:25.899
(You have to please the fans)

09:25.899 --> 09:27.319
(Clicked for her looks,
but she's actually good!)

09:27.319 --> 09:28.485
(Clicked for her looks, but she's actually good!)
All right. I'll play just a bit.

09:28.485 --> 09:30.028
(How about Pastel*Palettes?)
All right. I'll play just a bit.

09:30.028 --> 09:31.529
(Thanks for playing!)

09:42.207 --> 09:43.150
(I'm an octopus!)

09:43.150 --> 09:44.593
Another one?

09:49.964 --> 09:53.301
(How do I reply to
'My hair looks like an octopus'?)

09:57.722 --> 10:01.226
(Indeed, hair that looks
like an octopus can be a shock.)

10:12.737 --> 10:17.408
Is it the power? The connection?
Reconnecting it doesn't work.

10:17.408 --> 10:19.660
Why at a time like this?

10:20.160 --> 10:22.956
That's it! I'm replacing everything!

10:30.463 --> 10:31.464
(Delivery within 48 hours)

10:31.464 --> 10:33.174
(Delivery within 48 hours)
It's after the deadline.

10:34.384 --> 10:38.471
Ugh... That store
should be open in the morning...

10:39.472 --> 10:42.875
Oh, well. Guess I'll go to Akihabara.

10:43.809 --> 10:46.187
(Akihabara Station)

10:50.316 --> 10:52.026
(Viola:
Let's discuss your livestream)

10:52.026 --> 10:54.028
(I'm waiting for you at school)

11:15.925 --> 11:16.926
What?

11:17.719 --> 11:20.763
P... please... someone...

11:20.763 --> 11:21.931
A person?!

11:21.931 --> 11:25.184
Are you all right?
Can you say your name?

11:25.184 --> 11:30.440
No response! I can feel her pulse.
Is she breathing?

11:35.486 --> 11:37.697
Take this...

11:38.530 --> 11:40.325
Get me food...

11:40.325 --> 11:45.413
For the name
on the receipt... no need...

11:46.794 --> 11:49.255
Uh... Okay.

11:54.339 --> 11:55.965
(Receipt
Mrs. Noneed)

11:58.863 --> 12:00.448
Well, whatever.

12:01.530 --> 12:02.554
So...

12:05.266 --> 12:07.184
I thought a fresh one
would taste better.

12:07.894 --> 12:09.729
There's ketchup and mustard.

12:10.443 --> 12:12.028
It'll give you energy.

12:14.025 --> 12:16.319
All meat, huh?

12:24.118 --> 12:26.371
Thanks. You're a lifesaver.

12:27.247 --> 12:28.915
I'm glad.

12:43.537 --> 12:46.248
Don't you have to go to school?

12:47.058 --> 12:49.434
That's an Akiha uniform, right?

12:51.145 --> 12:56.067
Yes, I have to go, but...

12:56.776 --> 12:59.445
I've seen her somewhere...

13:05.827 --> 13:07.495
The "something" that's going on.

13:09.444 --> 13:11.566
Relationship problems?

13:14.419 --> 13:17.714
What do you think about model students?

13:17.714 --> 13:19.924
Why are you changing the subject?

13:24.929 --> 13:27.932
Well, it's their choice, really.

13:28.725 --> 13:31.936
But being around them could be annoying.

13:33.265 --> 13:34.641
I thought so.

13:36.732 --> 13:40.320
This is about a friend of mine, but...

13:40.320 --> 13:42.697
People really say that?

13:42.697 --> 13:45.742
My friend had a friend.

13:45.742 --> 13:47.493
My friend's friend

13:47.493 --> 13:50.203
was working with another friend,

13:50.203 --> 13:52.320
and my friend was asked to join.

13:52.320 --> 13:55.835
Sorry, I don't get it at all.
Can you make it simpler?

13:58.921 --> 14:00.715
Let's say my friend is a bear.

14:01.082 --> 14:02.089
Okay.

14:02.089 --> 14:05.215
And my friend's friend is a fennec.

14:05.215 --> 14:07.422
- A what?
- It's a type of fox.

14:07.422 --> 14:08.723
Oh.

14:08.723 --> 14:10.391
The bear was very proper.

14:10.391 --> 14:14.270
She was a dull presence,
unable to defy the atmosphere.

14:14.270 --> 14:16.606
And when the fennec was struggling,

14:17.269 --> 14:20.523
she couldn't do anything to help.

14:22.403 --> 14:25.865
She was a coward. A despicable coward.

14:25.865 --> 14:28.670
The fennec lost everything.

14:28.670 --> 14:30.411
The relationship's over.

14:31.204 --> 14:32.789
It's not over!

14:37.210 --> 14:39.670
Why don't you just do as you like?

14:45.593 --> 14:49.389
If you don't want it to end,
who cares about the facts?

14:52.392 --> 14:56.145
It wouldn't hurt so much
if it could just end.

14:56.813 --> 14:58.606
But that's not what you want.

15:00.525 --> 15:03.112
Anyway, eat this and cheer up.

15:03.112 --> 15:04.237
See you.

15:06.906 --> 15:09.242
Thank you, uh...

15:11.721 --> 15:13.598
The girl with the bone-in meat!

15:14.612 --> 15:15.905
Eat up.

15:17.985 --> 15:21.129
Are you ready to
release your cover song?

15:23.047 --> 15:24.632
Stop whining!

15:25.425 --> 15:28.219
But... it's just that...

15:28.719 --> 15:30.388
You don't like singing?

15:30.388 --> 15:33.224
No... I do like it.

15:33.224 --> 15:35.059
What about being in a group?

15:35.059 --> 15:36.686
Kind of...

15:36.686 --> 15:37.979
Is it showing your face?

15:37.979 --> 15:39.188
Yes.

15:40.481 --> 15:42.567
I'll let you in on a secret.

15:42.868 --> 15:44.193
A secret?

15:44.694 --> 15:46.320
If it's a video...

15:47.113 --> 15:49.073
If it's a video?

15:49.073 --> 15:51.909
You won't have to show your face!

15:51.909 --> 15:53.369
Oh, that's right!

15:53.369 --> 15:55.747
Will we finally hear Arale-chan sing?

15:55.747 --> 15:58.583
Will I be singing, then?

15:58.583 --> 16:00.251
Well, you're the vocalist.

16:00.251 --> 16:01.752
I guess you're right.

16:01.752 --> 16:04.839
I'm excited to hear you sing.

16:05.673 --> 16:10.761
But I haven't been singing recently,
so I'm a little rusty.

16:10.761 --> 16:16.851
So I can't really promise
I'll meet your expectations.

16:17.810 --> 16:19.479
Are you really excited?

16:19.479 --> 16:22.106
I'm so excited!

16:25.929 --> 16:29.155
H... how about you, Miyako-san?

16:29.155 --> 16:32.992
Huh? Oh, sure. I'm excited.

16:35.328 --> 16:41.380
W... well, then, maybe I could
try singing just once.

16:42.414 --> 16:43.461
That was easy.

16:43.461 --> 16:46.214
That's the spirit, Nakamachi-san!

16:46.214 --> 16:48.674
Anyway, about everyone's progress...

16:48.674 --> 16:50.801
Thanks for delivering the song!

16:51.344 --> 16:53.971
The client was thrilled they got
such an amazing song delivered so early.

16:53.971 --> 16:56.265
- So embarrassing! I went on about
- such an amazing song delivered so early.

16:56.265 --> 16:58.851
- determination and juggling two hats...
- Thanks.

16:58.851 --> 17:01.437
How utterly embarrassing.

17:01.437 --> 17:03.064
How about you, Miyanaga-san?

17:04.148 --> 17:06.465
I did it already!

17:06.465 --> 17:10.238
('Rainbow Soul Buster' Nono-chan Cover)
Oh, wow. The views look pretty good too!

17:10.238 --> 17:12.615
- I have an idea!
- What is it?

17:12.615 --> 17:17.744
I'm going to play guitar
for Arale-chan while she sings!

17:17.744 --> 17:18.996
Really?

17:18.996 --> 17:21.249
Sure!

17:21.249 --> 17:23.917
Yeah, that could work. On which song?

17:23.917 --> 17:28.172
Yuno-chan's song! I'm a longtime fan
since her band days!

17:28.714 --> 17:32.380
Yuno-chan!

17:32.380 --> 17:35.047
I love them all, so I'll play them all!

17:35.047 --> 17:38.022
Can I?

17:38.766 --> 17:42.109
I like the songs too, but...

17:42.109 --> 17:43.688
But what?

17:45.273 --> 17:46.816
I don't really...

17:47.724 --> 17:49.109
understand people.

17:49.109 --> 17:51.988
- I knew it! You're a robot!
- Unemployment?!

17:52.950 --> 17:54.440
M... Miyako-san!

17:54.440 --> 17:55.693
No, I'm not.

17:55.693 --> 17:57.287
I love the energy!

17:57.287 --> 18:00.580
Just decide what
you're going to sing, okay?

18:00.580 --> 18:01.955
Okay.

18:06.210 --> 18:07.420
I can sing.

18:08.160 --> 18:09.869
I can sing now.

18:15.803 --> 18:18.513
I can sing without showing my face!

18:18.513 --> 18:23.185
That means I'll be invincible!

18:23.185 --> 18:26.939
(Magical Physical Kululu Theme Song
'Good-Bye, Biceps')

18:37.032 --> 18:44.874
Why can birds fly through the sky?
Why are cats always asleep?

18:44.874 --> 18:48.753
How will you live today?

18:48.753 --> 18:56.552
All, all, all of it
Let's go search for it all

19:00.723 --> 19:08.522
Why does the morning sun kiss my skin?
Why does the night leave me feeling down?

19:08.522 --> 19:16.030
If only we could split our sorrows in half
Wouldn't that be great?

19:16.696 --> 19:23.996
Laughter and worry interweave
In a corner of this vast world

19:24.747 --> 19:33.089
Come with us
To uncover the wonders of the universe

19:34.048 --> 19:41.931
What stories shall we share today?
What melodies shall we sing?

19:41.931 --> 19:45.768
Even flowers as yet unseen

19:45.768 --> 19:52.983
All, all, all of it
Let's go search for it all

19:53.734 --> 20:00.782
All, all, all of it
Let's go search for it all

20:06.462 --> 20:08.791
I forgot to ask her name.

20:08.791 --> 20:10.584
I'm Marbled Meat.

20:10.584 --> 20:12.817
I wonder if she's from another country.

20:12.817 --> 20:15.464
I'm Juicymeat Chateaubriand.

20:15.464 --> 20:17.007
Hope we meet again.

20:17.007 --> 20:18.718
Next episode, "Might Be Fun."

20:18.718 --> 20:21.053
Delicious, together with you!

20:28.060 --> 20:31.397
I don't want it to end. That's why...

20:41.297 --> 20:44.785
Why would you go ahead
without me, Ritsu?

20:58.212 --> 20:59.964
Why...

21:01.010 --> 21:04.555
Aren't you happy to see me?

21:04.555 --> 21:06.724
You just hurt my feelings.

21:06.724 --> 21:10.978
You can't do that.
You have Fairy Bouquet.

21:10.978 --> 21:12.852
It's over with Arale-chan.

21:12.852 --> 21:13.981
No, it's not.

21:13.981 --> 21:15.816
You scare me.

21:15.816 --> 21:19.862
You're still going to see her,

21:19.862 --> 21:23.949
even though I keep
telling you not to go.

21:26.285 --> 21:29.914
Then, I guess it can't be helped.

21:31.457 --> 21:35.669
Did you know that humans
are the only animals that use fire?

21:37.421 --> 21:41.050
Civilization grew because
they weren't afraid of fire.

21:42.475 --> 21:44.053
Maybe that's why

21:44.804 --> 21:49.058
someone gets flamed
every day on the internet.

21:49.642 --> 21:51.310
It's funny, right?

21:51.310 --> 21:55.022
Once there's a spark,
all you have to do is watch.

21:57.775 --> 21:58.901
(Erea has the worst personality.)
(Scary)

22:00.903 --> 22:03.446
Here's the question!

22:03.446 --> 22:07.743
What do you think happens
when the spark burns out?

22:09.036 --> 22:10.913
Three...

22:11.475 --> 22:13.290
Two...

22:14.217 --> 22:16.278
One...

22:17.545 --> 22:19.296
Time's up.

22:21.257 --> 22:22.758
The answer is...

22:24.093 --> 22:26.136
everything around it burns!

22:26.637 --> 22:29.974
Friends, family, and...

22:29.974 --> 22:37.106
Uh, what was it again?
That one new group...

22:37.106 --> 22:39.316
Oh, right!

22:39.316 --> 22:42.486
Was it MewType?

22:44.488 --> 22:48.450
Back then, Arale-chan stayed quiet,

22:48.450 --> 22:51.871
so I figured that would be enough.

22:52.413 --> 22:55.875
But it's not over for her, huh?

22:57.209 --> 22:59.194
You may be right.

23:01.005 --> 23:03.132
She's not done yet, after all.

23:04.465 --> 23:07.261
Please stop.

23:07.261 --> 23:10.890
Well, well, well... what should I do?

23:12.337 --> 23:16.645
I promise I'll never talk to her again.

23:20.750 --> 23:22.961
Well done.

23:24.538 --> 23:26.205
As I thought,

23:27.573 --> 23:30.409
you're really the perfect model student.
